# U-Boot environment on the E1M-V2N / V2M eMMC: a redundant pair in boot
# partition 2 (Linux mmcblk0boot1; provisioning also writes the bootloader
# there, below these offsets). U-Boot imports only the OTA variables from it
# (CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST); anything else fw_setenv writes is ignored at
# boot. Linux's mmc0 is the on-module eMMC because e1m-v2n-som.dtsi aliases it
# so, whatever the carrier. Must match recipes-bsp/u-boot/u-boot/uboot-env-emmc.cfg
# (CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET / CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND / CONFIG_ENV_SIZE);
# and the SoM preset's on_module.emmc_boot.uboot_env;
# tests/scripts/test_uboot_env_layout.py enforces that.
# <device>            <offset>   <env size>
/dev/mmcblk0boot1     0x220000   0x10000
/dev/mmcblk0boot1     0x230000   0x10000
